ure practice</article-title><source>Health Educ Q</source><year>1993</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>391</fpage><lpage>408</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8307762</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glasgow</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Eakin</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name><name><surname>Toobert</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How generalizable are the results of diabetes self-management research? The impact of participation and attrition</article-title><source>Diabetes Educ</source><year>1996</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>573</fpage><lpage>2, 584</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8970287</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/014572179602200605</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Halm</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Penque</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Doll</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Beahrs</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Women and cardiac rehabilitation: referral and compliance patterns</article-title><source>J Cardiovasc Nurs</source><year>1999</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10098008</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marcus</surname><given-names>BH</given-names></name><name><surname>Nigg</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Riebe</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Forsyth</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interactive communication strategies: implications for population-based physical-activity promotion</article-title><source>A